# Flat screenprint: few colours, hard edges.
#
# Nearly all the work is in flattening the picture *before* it is reduced.
# Posterise a photograph directly and every stone and every leaf sits on a band
# boundary, so neighbouring pixels fall on opposite sides of it and the result
# is salt-and-pepper speckle rather than flat colour. At thumbnail size that
# speckle averages out and looks like a smooth tint, which is why this has to
# be judged at full size.
#
# Median removes the speckle but dissolves shapes if it is asked to do much, so
# it stays small and the surface blur does the flattening — it averages within
# a tolerance and leaves anything outside it alone, which is what keeps the
# edges of the stones while emptying their middles.
#
# Vibrance comes last. Applied before the reduction it widens the very channel
# gaps that quantising then doubles, so the colour it adds arrives as banding.

param levels = 6
param punch = 0.2
param flatten = 0.26

filter median radius={min*0.0045}
filter surface-blur radius={min*0.0325} threshold={flatten}
adjust levels black=0.04 white=0.96
adjust posterize levels={levels}
adjust vibrance vibrance={punch}
